
# Teaching Experience

## Associate Professor (Incoming Appointment)

### University of World Economy and Diplomacy (UWED), Tashkent, Uzbekistan

**September 2026 – May 2027**

I will teach graduate courses in International Economics, focusing on the theories, empirical evidence, and policy implications of international trade and global economic integration.

My teaching will cover key topics including international trade theories, trade policy, globalization, comparative advantage, trade and economic development, and the role of international economic relations in shaping economic growth and development outcomes.

---

# Teaching Philosophy

My teaching philosophy emphasizes connecting economic theories with real-world economic challenges and policy issues. I aim to help students understand how economic concepts can be applied to analyze global economic transformations, development challenges, inequality, and public policy decisions.

I encourage students to develop analytical thinking, empirical research skills, and the ability to critically evaluate economic evidence. Through the integration of theoretical frameworks and applied examples, I seek to create an engaging learning environment that helps students understand the practical relevance of economics.

